rsity L3: \nL4:  We gratefully acknowledge support from the Simons Foundation, cite1†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , and all contributors. cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org L5: \nL6: cite60†Image: arxiv logo > cite3†cs > arXiv:2509.21081v1\nL7: \nL8: cite4†Help†info.arxiv.org | cite5†Advanced Search L9: \nL10:  All fields Title Author Abstract Comments Journal reference ACM classification MSC classification Report number arXiv identifier DOI ORCID arXiv author ID Help pages Full text\nL11: \nL12: Search\nL13: cite61†Image: arXiv logo L14: \nL15: cite6† †www.cornell.edu L16: \nL17:  open search\nL18: \nL19: GO\nL20: \nL21: open navigation menu\nL22: ## quick links\nL23: \nL24:   * cite7†Login L25:   * cite4†Help Pages†info.arxiv.org L26:   * cite8†About†info.arxiv.org L27: \nL28: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL29: \nL30: arXiv:2509.21081v1 (cs)\nL31: \nL32: [Submitted on 25 Sep 2025]\nL33: # Title:TyphoonMLA: A Mixed Naive-Absorb MLA Kernel For Shared Prefix\nL34: \nL35: Authors:cite9†Ahmet Caner Yüzügüler , cite10†Ahmet Çelik , cite11†Jiawei Zhuang , cite12†Lukas Cavigelli L36: \nL37: View a PDF of the paper titled TyphoonMLA: A Mixed Naive-Absorb MLA Kernel For Shared Prefix, by Ahmet Caner Y\\\"uz\\\"ug\\\"uler and 3 other authors\nL38: \nL39: cite13†View PDF cite14†HTML (experimental) L40: > Abstract:Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA) is a recent attention mechanism adopted in state-of-the-art LLMs such as DeepSeek-v3 and Kimi K2. Thanks to its novel formulation, MLA allows two functionally equivalent but computationally distinct kernel implementations: naive and absorb.\nL41: While the naive kernels (e.g., FlashAttention) are typically preferred in training and prefill for their computational efficiency, existing decoding kernels (e.g., FlashMLA) rely on the absorb method to minimize HBM bandwidth usage. However, the compute-bound nature of the absorb implementations prohibits performance benefits from data reuse opportunities in attention calculations, such as shared prefixes.\nL42: In this work, we introduce TyphoonMLA, a hybrid approach that combines naive and absorb formulations to harness the strengths of both. TyphoonMLA effectively leverages the shared prefix by applying the naive formulation to the compute-bound parts of attention calculations, while reducing the bandwidth requirements for non-shared parts by using the absorb formulation.\nL43: As a result, TyphoonMLA improves the throughput of attention calculations in MLA architectures by up to 3x and 3.24x on NPU and GPUs, with only a 3% overhead in HBM size.\nL44: Subjects: Machine Learning (cs.LG); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL45: Cite as: cite15†arXiv:2509.21081 [cs.LG]\nL46:   (or  cite16†arXiv:2509.21081v1 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL47:   cite17†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2509.21081†doi.org L48: \nL49: Focus to learn more\nL50: \nL51:   arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL52: ## Submission history\nL53: \nL54: From: Ahmet Caner Yüzügüler [cite18†view email ]\nL55: [v1] Thu, 25 Sep 2025 12:32:02 UTC (278 KB)\nL56: \nL57: Full-text links:\nL58: ## Access Paper:\nL59: \nL60:  View a PDF of the paper titled TyphoonMLA: A Mixed Naive-Absorb MLA Kernel For Shared Prefix, by Ahmet Caner Y\\\"uz\\\"ug\\\"uler and 3 other authors\nL61: \nL62:   * cite13†View PDF L63:   * cite14†HTML (experimental) L64:   * cite19†TeX Source  L65: \nL66: cite20†view license L67: \nL68: Current browse context:\nL69: \nL70: cs.LG\nL71: \nL72: cite21†< prev |   cite22†next > L73: \nL74: cite23†new |  cite24†recent | cite25†2025-09 L75: \nL76: Change to browse by:\nL77: \nL78: cite26†cs L79: cite27†cs.AI L80: ### References & Citations\nL81: \nL82:   * cite28†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L83:   * cite29†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L84:   * cite30†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L85: \nL86: export BibTeX citation Loading...\nL87: \nL88: ## BibTeX formatte